Apache Grails IntelliJ Plugin Installation Guide
================================================

This document covers building the Apache Grails IntelliJ Plugin from a source
distribution. Most users should instead install the plugin from the JetBrains
Marketplace inside IntelliJ IDEA.

Requirements & Tooling Setup for Building
-----------------------------------------
Building requires a Java Development Kit (JDK) and Gradle (https://www.gradle.org).
A configuration file, `.sdkmanrc`, for SDKMAN! (https://sdkman.io) exists in the
source root with the recommended versions.

If SDKMAN! is installed, select the tooling by running the following command at
the source root:

        sdk env install

Otherwise, Gradle must be bootstrapped so that the correct version is used. The
source distribution ships without the Gradle Wrapper jar (per ASF source-release
policy), but it can be regenerated with any locally installed Gradle:

        cd gradle-bootstrap
        gradle bootstrap

This pins the wrapper to the version in `.sdkmanrc` and installs `gradlew` at the
source root. For the remaining commands: use `gradle` if tooling was installed
with SDKMAN! or `./gradlew` if the wrapper was bootstrapped.

Building
--------
Build the plugin distribution ZIP:

        ./gradlew buildPlugin

The ZIP is written to `build/distributions/` and can be installed in IntelliJ
IDEA via Settings > Plugins > Install Plugin from Disk.

Other useful tasks:

        ./gradlew check          # compile and run tests
        ./gradlew verifyPlugin   # IntelliJ Plugin Verifier
        ./gradlew rat            # Apache RAT license audit
        ./gradlew runIde         # launch a sandbox IDE with the plugin

Note: the build downloads the IntelliJ Platform (IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate) and
bundled plugins it compiles against; the first build requires network access and
several gigabytes of disk space.
